  "full_text": "So I guess I should put in my eight hours. Sometimes I just sit there going, why am I not recording? I don't know. I was getting too many, it was taking too long to upload, so now I'm going to do the lower resolution. There's no reason not to keep talking, I guess. So dirty dancing. Is my dancing too dirty, Mr. God? The young lions roared upon him and yelled, and they made the land waste. His cities are burned without inhabitants. Also the children of Noab and Tepab have broken the crown of thy head. Hast thou not procured this unto thyself, in that thou hast forsaken the Lord thy God, when he led thee by the way? And now what hast thou to do in the way of Egypt, to drink the waters of Syhor? Or what hast thou to do in the way of Assyria, to drink the waters of the river? Then on wickedness, shall correct thee, and thy backsliding shall reprove thee. Know therefore and see that it is an evil thing and bitter that thou hast forsaken the Lord thy God, and that fear of me is not in thee, saith the Lord God of hosts. For of old times I have broken thy yoke and burst thy bands, and thou sayest, I will not transgress when upon every high hill and under every green tree thou wanderest playing the harlot.",
